<%#- STRUCTURAL fork, and the sharpest of the three. Both styled variants mark
     the current page with a CLASS (btn-active, or a background utility). With
     no stylesheet there is nothing to carry that signal, so the current page
     has to change ELEMENT — <strong> rather than a styled <span> — and the
     inert prev/next markers become plain text. aria-current still does the work
     for a screen reader either way; what changes is that sighted users need the
     element, because there is no stylesheet to help. A class-token map cannot
     express a change of tag name. -%>
<%%# locals: (page: 1, page_count: 1) -%>
<%%# The numbered page control. It lives INSIDE the replaced fragment, like
    every other control in there: page_count is a server number, so a
    single-page list simply stops rendering this element.

    SCROLL. The links are anchors to the list, not buttons — the client only
    preventDefaults `submit`, so the click both performs the action and does the
    browser's own fragment jump. data-turbo="false" keeps Turbo Drive out of it.

    `on` returns a { data: } hash, so an element needing its OWN data attributes
    has to MERGE rather than splat, or the anchor stops scrolling. %>
<%%# PENDING. Nothing here asks for it: the client stamps data-hibiki-busy on
    the control that fired, so the clicked page link dims itself while the trip
    is out, and the swap that answers it destroys the attribute along with the
    link. The bar above the list is the other half — the anchor jump has
    already put it in view by then. %>
<%% page_data = ->(n) { { turbo: false }.merge(on(:go_to_page, with: { page: n })[:data]) } %>
<%%# The id-carrying wrapper always renders, so idiomorph always has a node to
    pair with. %>
<div id="<%= pagination_dom_id %>">
  <%% if page_count > 1 %>
    <nav aria-label="Pagination">
      <%%# Prev/next stay rendered and go inert at the ends rather than
          disappearing, so the control keeps its position across a page change.
          A span, not a disabled link: there is no page to name, so there is no
          action to stamp. %>
      <%% if page == 1 %>
        <span aria-disabled="true">«</span>
      <%% else %>
        <%%= link_to "«", "#<%= list_dom_id %>", rel: "prev",
                    "aria-label": "Previous page", data: page_data.(page - 1) %>
      <%% end %>

      <%% <%= query_class_name %>.page_numbers(page: page, page_count: page_count).each do |n| %>
        <%% if n.nil? %>
          <span aria-hidden="true">…</span>
        <%% elsif n == page %>
          <strong aria-current="page"><%%= n %></strong>
        <%% else %>
          <%%= link_to n, "#<%= list_dom_id %>", "aria-label": "Page #{n}", data: page_data.(n) %>
        <%% end %>
      <%% end %>

      <%% if page == page_count %>
        <span aria-disabled="true">»</span>
      <%% else %>
        <%%= link_to "»", "#<%= list_dom_id %>", rel: "next",
                    "aria-label": "Next page", data: page_data.(page + 1) %>
      <%% end %>
    </nav>
  <%% end %>
</div>
